cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "umud-pixel-vote: a specialised orientation head for muscle ultrasound, with its own refutations"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Angulo de Lafuente"
    given-names: "Francisco"
    alias: "Agnuxo1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Agnuxo1/umud-pixel-vote"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - muscle-ultrasound
  - pennation-angle
  - fascicle-length
  - muscle-thickness
  - image-segmentation
  - physical-scale-recovery
  - neural-cellular-automata
  - ablation-study
abstract: >-
  Code and measurements for the UMUD Challenge (Muscle Architecture in Ultrasound Data).
  NeuroPixelField is a specialised orientation head: given the true fascicle mask it measures
  fascicle orientation to 1.42 +/- 0.23 degrees on the 512x512 fold, three times better than a
  control with 33 times more parameters, over three seeds. Without that mask it is the worst of
  the four arms, and on muscle thickness it is the worst in all five folds, so the capability is
  a component's and not the finished system's. Around it: physical scale recovered from the
  scanner's own ruler without OCR, and a geometry stage verified to 0.1 degrees. Two
  methodological findings are reported in full: the training loss orders the architectures
  backwards with respect to the millimetres and degrees the task is scored on, and the ablation
  margin on muscle thickness does not survive its own seed noise, which retracted this work's
  own earlier headline. The repository contains no competition data.
